{
  "_why": "A charted map at the width a view has to survive: twenty-eight children, eleven sources with dependents behind them and nine with none, against later ranks of four, two, one and one. Every other fixture here is small enough that one row holds it, so nothing in the tree asked what happens when a single rank is wider than the window. #224 waits on #499, which is not a child of this map and so is a fact about that ticket rather than an edge on the canvas. #212 is closed and cut, in a sentence far too long for a plate the width of the others; #215 is unclassified, #217 is a spec child that would otherwise be takeable, and the fog was surveyed.",
  "data": {
