      "issue": {
        "number": 200,
        "title": "Spec: the wide map",
        "state": "OPEN",
        "body": "## Notes\n\nTwenty-eight tickets charted in one pass, and the width is the point: eleven of\nthe sources feed the four ranks behind them, and nine of them feed nothing.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- #212 - the desktop shell already ships a tray icon on every platform this project supports, so a second one here would have meant maintaining both of them for the rest of the run and answering to whichever one the operator happened to be looking at\n\n## Not yet specified\n\n- How a rank wider than the window is read on a small screen\n- Whether the rank a node sits on is worth a number beside it\n  - and whether that number survives a cycle\n- What a fan-out of eleven looks like when nine of the eleven feed nothing\n\n## Decisions so far\n\n- The map draws in the operator's own drag order, never in a ranking of its own.\n",
        "url": "https://github.com/o/r/issues/200",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-05T09:12:44Z",
